<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01875</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ccd2fb80-7bba-4c12-a249-e61e33f072d2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_13e5d43f-0171-4ebf-bf68-39abef4954ec" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Choose the expression that best describes the diagram.
          
          <figure id="fig-00001"><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_10_01.jpg"/></media></para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+5x+8\).</para>
            <para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+14x + 23\).</para>
            <para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para>
            <para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(30x^2\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_279bb73a-6893-4a2d-b527-807bee0fa839" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>In questions a–d, match each expanded quadratic expression with an equivalent expression written as a product.</para>
            <para>\(x^2+12x+32\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \((x+8)(x+4)\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8e7633c5-78da-49c3-b6a7-e6265f139b84" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> \(x^2+5x+6\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \((x+2)(x+3)\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5d9dd332-aeb9-4237-affe-cd381e9dd585" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x^2+6x+8\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is:\((x+4)(x+2)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_224fe3bf-30c3-4dc2-a62b-aaa67c1a3c84" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x^2+8x+12\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para>
            <para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+6)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is:\((x+2)(x+6)\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a598cde7-4fc5-490f-833a-0b5c704e9fcf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> expressions that are equivalent to \(x^2+4x\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x(x+4)\), \((x+2)^2-4\), \((x+4)x\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.8.2-7.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x(x+4)\), \((x+2)^2-4\), \((x+4)x\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5fc3f3a4-158c-4131-977c-33bba99944f5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>

            <para>Tyler drew a diagram to expand \((x+5)(2x+3)\).</para>
            <para> Tyler’s diagram is incorrect. Choose the sentence that describes Tyler’s mistake.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them.</para>
            <para>Tyler multiplied 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of adding them.</para>
            <para>Tyler should have labeled the top \(2x\) and 5 and the side \(x\) and 3.</para>
            <para>Tyler should have labeled the top \(x\) and 3 and the side \(2x\) and 5.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.
     </para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_740ac6b4-bf17-4ecd-ae4e-ae1e88a74c1f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> What is the correct expanded form of \((x+5)(2x+3)\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(3x+8\)</para>
            <para>\(30x^2\)</para>
            <para>\(2x^2+10x+8\)</para>
            <para>\(2x^2+13x+15\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(2x^2+13x+15\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is : \(2x^2+13x+15\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
